# Cursor Project Rules (Laravel — Full-Stack)

## Principles
- KISS, DRY, Separation of Concerns, SOLID.
- **No business logic in controllers.**
- **Validate with Form Requests** only.
- **Use Actions/Services + Repositories** for domain + data access.
- **Use Blade components/partials** to remove repetition.
- Follow Laravel/PSR-12 naming & structure. English comments only.
- Follow the standard of Modules, and make all routes and repositories and blades inside the Modules that it's related to.

## Controllers (thin)
- Accept FormRequest, delegate to an **Action/Service**, return view/resource.
```php
public function store(\App\Http\Requests\Tag\StoreTagRequest $request,
                      \App\Actions\Tag\CreateTagAction $action)
{
    $tag = $action->handle($request->validated());
    return redirect()->route('tags.show', $tag)->with('status','Created');
}
